          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal H$ carry an irreducible positive unitary super-Poincare representation with metric $\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)$, future-cone support and the charge-domain reduction conditions stated in its definition. Let $\\mathcal C_+^*$ be the closed future cone from the representation definition and define $s:\\mathcal C_+^*\\to[0,\\infty)$ by $s(p)=-\\eta^{\\mu\\nu}p_\\mu p_\\nu$. For Borel $A\\subseteq[0,\\infty)$ define $F(A)=E(\\{p\\in\\mathcal C_+^*:s(p)\\in A\\})$. Then every supercharge and its adjoint reduce each mass-squared spectral subspace: if $\\psi\\in D(Q)\\cap\\operatorname{ran}F(A)$ then $Q\\psi\\in\\operatorname{ran}F(A)$, and the same holds for $Q^*$. Moreover there is a unique $m^2\\ge0$ such that $F(A)=I$ when $m^2\\in A$ and $F(A)=0$ when $m^2\\notin A$. Thus the nonnegative mass $m=\\sqrt{m^2}$ is constant throughout the irreducible multiplet. Use natural units $\\hbar=c=1$, so $m$ has mass dimension one and $m^2$ has mass dimension two. For a nonzero supercharge image, the source and image lie in the same mass spectral sector. No sharp-momentum eigenvector or rest frame is assumed in the full Hilbert space. If an additional group acts unitarily and commutes with the supercharges on their invariant domains, each supercharge also intertwines that group action; no gauge-charge conclusion is asserted without this extra hypothesis.",
