          "statement": "For the basis-indexed vector space and product $e_Se_T=0$ when $S\\cap T\\ne\\varnothing$ and $e_Se_T=(-1)^{\\nu(S,T)}e_{S\\cup T}$ otherwise, with $\\nu(S,T)=|\\{(s,t)\\in S\\times T:s>t\\}|$, multiplication is associative, unital and supercommutative. The graded tensor product with a supercommutative coefficient algebra is also associative and supercommutative. The basis formulas for left and right odd differentiation extend to derivations with the stated Leibniz rules. The ordered four-variable Berezin integral is a well-defined linear functional extracting the coefficient of $\\theta^1\\theta^2\\bar\\theta^{\\dot1}\\bar\\theta^{\\dot2}$, and the stated conjugation is an involutive anti-automorphism.",
