+# Batch 54 authoring notes — Hall Wall Crossing and Physical BPS Dictionary
+
+Run: `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`  
+Batch: 54  
+Scope: `qftx-physical-hall-bps-wall-crossing` and its examples companion only.
+
+## Plan and inventory
+
+The complete design at `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md:751` matches the corresponding `plan-spec.json` row: title, category/library, order 1010, A/B pairing, and the A-page requirements `qftx-bps-indices`, `qftx-susy-moduli-and-dualities`, and `qftx-hall-bps-wall-crossing`. There is no plan-spec conflict. The design names two A items; the binding authoring direction also requires substantive B examples, so the B page contains `ex-qftx-physical-bps-kronecker-hall-sector` without changing the shared plan.
+
+The existing run dependency file lists batch 54 at level 7 with page prerequisites from batches 33 and 53. After inspecting the current prerequisite statements, this batch adds a direct item edge from the charge-data definition to `def-qftx-bps-state-and-saturation` in batch 29. Its item level is 4; the existing level-8 SW postulate remains the maximum in-run supplier of the charge-data item, so item levels are 9, 10, and 11 for charge data, transport theorem, and example. The batch level remains 7, but the direct batch prerequisite set now also includes batch 29. `batch-dependency-levels.mjs check` must be rerun by the owner after the run manifests are loadable; the shared scheduling file was not edited.
+
+The output manifest has the two planned A items and one B example. Both page files contain YAML frontmatter only and have empty Markdown bodies. The new charge-data dependencies are `def-countable-choice`, the current Coulomb-branch definition and Seiberg–Witten postulate, `def-qftx-bps-state-and-saturation`, and the two trace-class definitions. The theorem uses the charge datum and the finite-field Hall generator and invariance proposition. The example uses the charge datum, theorem, finite-quiver stability data, Hall generator, phase-sum lemma, and Hall invariance proposition. Their dependency levels are computed from their actual current-run suppliers.
+
+## Current supplier and interface audit
+
+`loadStep1Record` and `step1Decision` were rerun against the current carriers. The batch-33 Coulomb-branch definition and Seiberg–Witten postulate are ready. `def-qftx-bps-state-and-saturation` in batch 29 is ready and states the exact massive-fiber condition: in the N=2 case, saturation is $M=|z|$ and the two specified annihilating supercharge combinations vanish. The batch-53 carrier `def-qftx-physical-bps-index` is present and its current Step-1 record is ready.
+
+The full batch-53 definition was inspected. It defines a pure-point graded Witten heat supertrace $W_E(\beta)$ and says a model may call its kernel a BPS index only after its own supercharge algebra identifies that kernel with the specified saturated sector. It does not define the GMN second-helicity $B_2$ trace. This pair therefore defines $B_2$ locally on a supplied saturated one-particle sector, with a supplied Hilbert basis and bounded trace-class insertion, and cites the actual BPS-saturation and trace-class suppliers. It does not identify $W_E(\beta)$ with $B_2$ and does not assert that the model supplies such a sector. The page-level dependency was checked and recorded as verified with this distinction in `batch-54.cross-batch-dependencies.json`.
+
+The finite-field Hall supplier is a mathematical input only. The published `prop-qftx-hall-spectrum-invariance` statement and complete relevant proof chain were inspected, along with the current owner Hall review in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/hall-review.md`. That review finds the finite-field chain sound at its stated scope; it is not relabelled as independent proof approval. The Hall items use finite acyclic quivers, finite fields, degreewise groupoids, and completed Euler/skew tori. They provide no physical Hilbert-space or BPS-index identification.
+
+## Authored items and claim boundary
+
+`def-qftx-physical-bps-charge-data` defines the regular-patch pure-SU(2) label lattice, source-normalized scalar central charge, DSZ form, monopole/dyon labels and two-arrow orientation, supplied saturated one-particle sector, $B_2$ index, support, walls, phases, cone, and degree. Conventions are $c=\hbar=1$, $z=\sqrt2(n_ea+n_ma_D)$, and $\langle(n_e,n_m),(n'_e,n'_m)\rangle=2(n_mn'_e-n_en'_m)$, so the selected monopole/dyon pairing is $+2$. The item states the Hilbert, gap, trace-class and basis requirements as model data; it claims no state existence, local constancy, or Hall identification.
+
+`pthm-qftx-physical-bps-wall-crossing` is a conditional transport theorem. It states the coefficient embedding, charge and pairing maps, degree compatibility, phase order, sign refinement, completed tori, and continuous per-phase bridge. Its proof checks the formal KS automorphisms and torus map, applies the inspected finite-field Hall invariance proposition, and transports equality through the exact bridge. The bridge remains an explicit additional physical hypothesis; the theorem does not prove that the selected SU(2) model supplies it.
+
+`ex-qftx-physical-bps-kronecker-hall-sector` counts the two-arrow dimension-(1,1) representations over $\mathbb F_q$: one zero orbit, $q+1$ nonzero projective orbits, stabilizers $(q-1)^2$ and $q-1$, and stable Hall coefficient $(q+1)/(q-1)$ in the specified strict chamber because $\chi_Q((1,1),(1,1))=0$. The reversed strict chamber has no semistable object of that dimension. The TikZ quiver diagram repeats the stated orientation; the proof is algebraic and does not rely on the diagram. The rational groupoid weight is explicitly not identified with $B_2$.
+
+The model-specific Hall-to-$B_2$ bridge is still unproved. No count identification is made without it. If the owner requires an unconditional physical dictionary, the proposed addition is a separate A-page theorem specifying and proving a model-specific map from the selected physical Hilbert-space index to the finite-field Hall phase factors; the finite-field suppliers and the Witten-index item do not supply that result. The current pair remains fully conditional and makes no unconditional physical claim.
+
+## Sources and retrieval evidence
+
+Four full-text sources were read for the A page; their exact item-level support, limitations, harvest dispositions, searches, retrieval attempts and stamps are in `batch-54-source-coverage.json` and `batch-54.coverage.json`.
+
+- N. Seiberg and E. Witten, `https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9407087v1`, full 45-page PDF: Section 1 equations (1.1)–(1.2), Section 4 equations (4.3)–(4.9), and Section 6 equations (6.19)–(6.28). Supports the source normalization, periods and alignment discussion; does not make every formal charge a realized stable state.
+- David Tong, `https://davidtong.org/pdfs/teaching/supersymmetric-field-theory/susy.pdf`, full 237-page lecture notes: §2.4.2, printed pp. 40–41. Supports the massive N=2 central-charge bound and shortened representations; its normalization is not substituted for Seiberg–Witten's.
+- Frederik Denef, `https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0206072`, full 47-page paper: §5.3, printed pp. 35–36. Supports the pure-SU(2) monopole/dyon quiver motivation and pairing magnitude 2; its complex quiver moduli are not the finite-field groupoid used in the local example.
+- Davide Gaiotto, Gregory W. Moore, and Andrew Neitzke, `https://arxiv.org/pdf/0807.4723`, full 66-page paper: Introduction equation (1.1), §§2.1–2.2, and opening of §7. Supports the $B_2$ and KS conventions and the support qualification; it does not prove the finite-field Hall-to-Hilbert bridge.
+
+All four source fetch stamps passed: SW 45 pages, `7ef9d9ef18ee33e3`; Tong 237 pages, `1629f49d443adec5`; Denef 47 pages, `876aa16f987367d3`; GMN 66 pages, `e41d9f3d37ac2f78`. No retrieval failure or recovery retry occurred. The full-text searches and per-item dispositions are retained in the source-coverage evidence; no source-resolution drop or owner-escalation record was needed.
+
+## Validation and remaining owner action
+
+Scoped batch-54 checks passed: precheck (3 items, 2 proof-bearing, 0 failures); depcheck (3 assigned items and their prerequisite closure, 0 errors or warnings); rendercheck (3 items and 2 pages, 0 errors or warnings); proof layout (3 items, 10 steps, 0 defects); strict proof contracts (all 3 items); coverage checklist (2 pages, 17 harvested results, 0 errors or warnings); source fetch (4/4 unique A-page sources stamped, 7/7 page-source records fetch-verified, 0 drops); and manifest dependency declarations (3 items, 0 missing dependency arrays). The two YAML page files have no Markdown body. The local batch manifest contains 2 pages and 3 complete item declarations. All three assigned items have current Step-1 `ready` records; the conditional bridge remains explicitly unproved and is not treated as a supplied physical fact.
+
+The full-run `proof-contract-coverage` check stops on the unrelated empty inventory `qftx-s3-partition-functions`; that page is outside this batch and was not edited. The full-run manifest reader also stops on an invalid/empty page inventory in batch 49. The run-wide `batch-dependency-levels.mjs check` reports stale shared scheduling metadata. A read-only recomputation gives batch 54 level 7 with direct batch prerequisites 29, 33, and 53; the existing shared record lists only 33 and 53. The new item edge to `def-qftx-bps-state-and-saturation` is documented in the scoped cross-batch file. The owner must reconcile `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-dependency-levels.json`; it was left unchanged as shared scheduling state.
+
+The six scoped cross-batch rows are verified interface checks, not independent proof approvals. The only unresolved scientific extension is a model-specific Hall-to-$B_2$ bridge. If an unconditional physical dictionary is required, the proposed follow-up is a separate A-page theorem proving that map under explicit model inputs; this pair neither supplies nor claims that result.
